# ============================================================================
# deploy/caddy/maintenance-server.caddy — the loopback static server for the maintenance page
# (B485; installed by deploy/install-maintenance-page.sh, imported at TOP LEVEL of the Caddyfile)
#
# Why a second listener instead of file_server inside handle_errors: measured on Caddy v2.11.9, a
# file_server inside an error handler answers 5xx with an EMPTY body (the handler fails and the error
# status is rendered again), while a plain reverse_proxy to this listener serves the page correctly.
#
# Bound to loopback only; it is not reachable from outside the host and carries no secrets.
# The directory is /etc/caddy/maintenance on purpose: the panel's data dir /var/lib/skygate is
# 0750 skygate:skygate BY DESIGN, and the caddy service user could not traverse into it — the first
# install proved it by taking the site down with "Failed to import … permission denied".
# ============================================================================

http://127.0.0.1:8081 {
	root * /etc/caddy/maintenance
	file_server
}
